    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Student-Research-Assistant_JR0000080273": {
      "title": "Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). POSITION SUMMARY The MScPH Program Office within the Department of Epidemiology, Biostatistics and Occupational Health is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Student Research Assistant to support a project examining the newly released Core Competencies for Public Health in Canada. The successful candidate will conduct a systematic analysis of the competencies and assist with mapping the MScPH program research and training components against the new framework. This position offers an excellent opportunity for a graduate student to develop skills in competency mapping, qualitative analysis, and educational program evaluation while working closely with the MScPH Program Director. RESPONSIBILITIES Assist in a research project examining the alignment of the MScPH curriculum with the new Core Competencies for Public Health in Canada. Participate in the preparation of research documentation, including the development of a competency-matching rubric. Assist with the compilation and organization of research data by creating and populating a spreadsheet-based mapping matrix. Assist with the analysis and interpretation of competency framework and curriculum data to identify areas of alignment and gaps. Participate in regular meetings with the MScPH Program Director and contribute to project updates and discussions. Perform various administrative and project-related tasks in support of the research initiative. QUALIFICATIONS Current McGill graduate student. Experience with research projects, program evaluation, curriculum review, or competency-based education. Experience organizing and analyzing qualitative information. Strong analytical and critical thinking skills. Excellent attention to detail and ability to work independently. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and other productivity software. Strong written and verbal communication skills in English. Completion of the first year of MScPH coursework is an asset. Hiring Unit: Department of Epidemiology, Biostatistics and Occupational Health Number of Positions: 1 Supervisor: Professor Jan Cooper Total Hours Per Week: Up to 10 hours per week (part-time) Hourly Salary: $25 Location: 2001 McGill College « Connaissance du français et de l'anglais: L'Université McGill est une université de langue anglaise où les tâches quotidiennes peuvent nécessiter une communication verbale et écrite en anglais.  Le niveau d’anglais requis pour ce poste a été déterminé comme étant de niveau #4 (qualificatif) sur une échelle de 0-4.» “Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4.” In accordance with Canadian and Quebec law, the present offer is conditional upon your obtaining the appropriate work authorization from any or all of the following as applicable: Citizenship & Immigration Canada, Immigration Quebec and Human Resources & Skills Development Canada (HRSDC). Hourly Salary: $25.00 Hours per Week: 10 (Part time) Location: McGill College 2001 Supervisor: Assistant Professor (Teaching) Position Start Date: 2026-09-04 Position End Date: 2027-03-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-15 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Adams-Building/Course-Lecturer-AERO-410_JR0000080329-1": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer AERO 410",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). AFFICHAGE DE COURS, CHARGÉE DE COURS/INSTRUCTEUR(TRICE) COURSE POSTING, COURSE LECTURER/INSTRUCTOR Unité d’embauche / Hiring Unit: McGill Institute for Aerospace Engineering Titre de cours / Course Title: Aerospace Design and Certification Process Single / Subject Code: AERO 410 Session / Term: Hiver 2027 / Winter 2027 Endroit / Location: McGill Centre-Ville / McGill Downtown Campus Horaire / Schedule: Mercredi de 17h35 à 20h25 / Wednesday 5:35 p.m. to 8:25 p.m. Préparation et Sessions de Cours / Preparation and Course Lectures: 5 janvier à 14 avril, 2027 / January 5 to April 14, 2027 Compensation : $11,479 Exigences de qualification pour l’enseignement / Teaching Qualification Requirements: Éducation / Education: Minimum of Master’s degree in Engineering; ideally member of order of engineers. Expérience / Experience: Minimum of ten years’ experience in aerospace certification and design. Autre(s) exigence(s) de qualifications/Other qualification requirement(s): Extensive experience with Aerospace Engineering design and engineering team management. Demonstrated knowledge of spoken and written English. Strong problem-solving skills and flexible approach to teaching. Enseignement partagé / Team teaching: No/Non Si oui, nombre de crédits/CEUs If yes, number of credits/CEUs: 3 credits The University may, at its discretion, assign the person of its choice to give this course/teaching. L’université possède la discrétion d’assigner la personne de son choix pour donner ce Cours/Enseignement. Hiring Unit: McGill Institute for Aerospace Engineering Course Title: Aerospace Design and Certification Process Subject Code: AERO 410 001 Location: TBA Schedule: Wednesday 5:35 pm to 8:25 pm Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
